.SS "static void julia_iterations (\fBt_render_vars\fP * vars, \fBt_data\fP * data)\fC [static]\fP"

.PP
Performs the iterations for a signle point in the Julia set\&. This function applies the Julia set formula iteratively to determine whether a given point escapes the threshold\&. The number of iterations taken before escape determines the point's color\&.
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBCore Algorithm:\fP The formula \fCz = z^2 + c\fP is applied, where:
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fCz\fP is a complex number, represented by real (\fCz_re\fP) and imaginary (\fCz_im\fP) parts\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
\fCc\fP is a constant defined by the user (real and imaginary parts)\&.
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBBounding Condition:\fP The iteerations stop when:
.IP "  \(bu" 4
The sum of the squares of the real and imaginary parts exceeds 4\&.0\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
The maximum number of iterations (\fCMAX_ITERATIONS\fP) is reached\&.
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBOptimization:\fP Squared values (\fCz_re^2\fP and \fCz_im^2\fP) are cached to avoid redundant calculations\&.
.PP
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvars\fP Pointer to the structure holding rendering variables (e\&.g\&., \fCz\fP and \fCiterations\fP)\&. @params data Pointer to the main fractal data, including the Julia constant (\fCc\fP)\&. 
.RE
.PP

