.SS "void render_julia (\fBt_data\fP * data)"

.PP
Renders the Julia set fractal\&. Renders the Julia fractal\&.
.PP
This function handles the full rendering process for the Julia set by iterating through all rows of the screen, rendering each row sequentially\&.
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBSetup:\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Calculates the scaling and starting coordinates based on the zoom level and positional offsets provided by the user\&.
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBRow-by-Row Rendering:\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
For each row on the screen (\fCy\fP coordinate), the corresponding imaginary coordinate is computed\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
The row is passed to \fCrender_julia_row\fP, which handles the pixel-by-pixel rendering\&.
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBFull Image Construction:\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
The ffunction processes every row until the entire fractal is rendered\&.
.PP

.PP
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdata\fP Pointer to the main fractal data structure, including rendering details such as zoom, offsets, and fractal paarameters\&. 
