.SS "static void render_julia_row (\fBt_render_vars\fP * vars, \fBt_data\fP * data, int y)\fC [static]\fP"

.PP
Renders a single row of the Julia set\&. This function processes one row of the pixel in the Juliaa set by iterating through each pixel, applying the Juliaa set formula, and determining its color\&.
.PP
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBCoordinate Mapping:\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
Each pixel is mapped to a complex number (\fCz\fP) based on its position and the scaling factors calculated from the zoom and offsets\&.
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBIteration and Coloring:\fP
.IP "  \(bu" 4
The Julia set formula is applied iteratively for each pixel\&.
.IP "  \(bu" 4
The number of iterations is used to calculate the pixel's color\&.
.PP

.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBRow Processing:\fP Each pixel in the row is processed sequentially, and the result is stored in the image buffer\&.
.PP
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIvars\fP Pointer to the rendering variables structure (e\&.g\&., pixel and scaling)\&. 
.br
\fIdata\fP Pointer to the main fractal data\&. 
.br
\fIy\fP The current row index being processed (0 for the first row, up to \fCHEIGHT - 1\fP)\&. 
.RE
.PP

